00:39:34.835 --> 00:39:36.950
are there instances
of not having enough

00:39:38.000 --> 00:39:38.840
soldier data,

00:39:42.020 --> 00:39:45.155
and how currently is HRC
collecting that data?

00:39:47.570 --> 00:39:49.130
- I'm sorry, go ahead. I
don't want to cut you off.

00:39:49.730 --> 00:39:51.020
- And just to continue on,

00:39:51.020 --> 00:39:54.155
how does your team handle
when there's not enough data?

00:39:55.230 --> 00:39:56.780
- So we have a ton of data,

00:39:56.780 --> 00:39:58.265
doesn't necessarily mean
it's the right data.

00:39:59.270 --> 00:40:01.130
And as we're going
through these models,

00:40:01.130 --> 00:40:03.320
that was actually what
kicked off our assessment program.

00:40:03.320 --> 00:40:08.190
I don't have enough in people's
files to be able to say what

00:40:08.190 --> 00:40:12.150
their talent attributes are.
And so we go over to our

00:40:12.150 --> 00:40:13.920
research entities at the
Army Research Institute,

00:40:13.920 --> 00:40:15.340
Army Research
labs and say, hey,

00:40:15.340 --> 00:40:18.030
you guys got any kind of
existing studies that we can

00:40:18.030 --> 00:40:20.370
peel a couple things off
of and take a look at,

00:40:20.370 --> 00:40:22.860
and maybe experiment, and
go collect some more data

00:40:23.670 --> 00:40:24.840
with you guys on this.

00:40:24.840 --> 00:40:27.190
And we've had a really
