00:40:56.430 --> 00:40:58.600
fully off during that time.

00:40:58.600 --> 00:41:01.305
And I saw you were asking
some advice to other people

00:41:02.310 --> 00:41:05.490
from your LinkedIn network
too. And I was just wondering

00:41:06.120 --> 00:41:08.190
what your thoughts
are on that and what

00:41:08.930 --> 00:41:11.745
you're learning from
your own network too.

00:41:12.390 --> 00:41:14.310
- Well, that's the fun
part about this network.

00:41:14.310 --> 00:41:17.040
I love throwing questions out there
and just saying, hey, guys, I'm human.

00:41:17.700 --> 00:41:19.170
I do a lot of things right.

00:41:19.170 --> 00:41:20.610
And I've been put in
a position because--

00:41:21.315 --> 00:41:23.820
you can wave your awesome
flag all day but it's also,

00:41:23.820 --> 00:41:25.570
I screw up a lot of things.

00:41:25.570 --> 00:41:27.270
I am horrible at
taking time off.

00:41:28.830 --> 00:41:31.500
I will compulsively go
and check things if not--

00:41:31.500 --> 00:41:32.800
I've got Mike [? Carroll, ?]

00:41:32.800 --> 00:41:34.350
who's our lead for procurement,

00:41:34.350 --> 00:41:36.630
but he's also my accountability
buddy. He's just like,

00:41:36.630 --> 00:41:39.090
I see you. I see you on
Teams, get off, go home.

00:41:40.500 --> 00:41:44.160
So I love throwing things like
that out to the community and

00:41:44.160 --> 00:41:45.270
just saying, hey,

00:41:45.270 --> 00:41:47.130
I'm not the only person
who's dealing with this.

00:41:47.130 --> 00:41:49.470
And this is a professional
wellness thing.

00:41:49.470 --> 00:41:52.380
And I think all of us can
benefit from the discussion on.

00:41:52.380 --> 00:41:54.720
Let me throw it out there. You
guys tell me what works for you.

00:41:54.720 --> 00:41:57.390
And a lot of it came back
that same thing. It's like,

00:41:57.390 --> 00:42:02.085
we need that time to
do an active or inactive recharge.

00:42:02.700 --> 00:42:05.430
Sometimes, it's doing
yoga or cross training.

00:42:05.430 --> 00:42:08.040
When you've been trying
to ramp up for a race,

00:42:08.670 --> 00:42:10.680
you've got to do something
but make it something that's not

00:42:10.680 --> 00:42:11.870
work. So

00:42:12.480 --> 00:42:14.610
trying to figure out those
good substitutions or those

00:42:14.610 --> 00:42:15.525
complementary activities.

00:42:15.525 --> 00:42:18.240
And we talked earlier about was
one of my favorite things to

00:42:18.240 --> 00:42:20.910
do, not at work. I love
hiking, love cooking,

00:42:20.910 --> 00:42:22.320
love going to the beach.

00:42:22.320 --> 00:42:25.020
And I think we've got to
let ourselves know that not only is

00:42:25.020 --> 00:42:26.340
it OK to have hobbies,

00:42:26.340 --> 00:42:27.990
not everything has to
be work and hustle.

00:42:27.990 --> 00:42:31.470
But those things actually
complement your ability to

00:42:31.470 --> 00:42:32.955
refresh, recharge,
and do your job.

00:42:34.140 --> 00:42:37.080
So I think it's hugely
important and I'm always trying

00:42:37.080 --> 00:42:38.700
to figure out ways
to get better at it.

00:42:39.900 --> 00:42:43.610
- I love that idea of having
an accountability buddy too.

00:42:43.610 --> 00:42:46.790
And when we see
our friends at work

00:42:47.660 --> 00:42:49.220
